<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sumy is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and the centre of Sumy Oblast, on the Psel river close to the Russian border. It was founded in the 1650s by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> settlers from right-bank Ukraine under Herasym Kondratiev and became the seat of the Sumy Cossack regiment of Sloboda Ukraine. In the 19th century it grew into a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sumy.jpg" alt="Sumy" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Максим Бондаревский · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_of_Sumy_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
